WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.169 --> 00:00:04.450
Our Introduction to Optimization tutorial series

2
00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:05.849
is first going to start by having

3
00:00:05.849 --> 00:00:09.929
us take a look at how we think about optimization

4
00:00:09.929 --> 00:00:13.289
throughout the lifetime of our Unreal Engine 5 projects.

5
00:00:13.289 --> 00:00:16.210
We'll then move on to ways we can optimize our projects

6
00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:19.089
right from our project's initial creation.

7
00:00:19.089 --> 00:00:21.829
We'll then take a look at how we can optimize our texture

8
00:00:21.829 --> 00:00:25.730
content, as well as optimize both static and skeletal mesh

9
00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:27.239
content.

10
00:00:27.239 --> 00:00:29.579
We'll then have a look at how we can use Unreal's

11
00:00:29.579 --> 00:00:33.619
materials systems to help optimize our material, as well

12
00:00:33.619 --> 00:00:35.920
as our material workflow.

13
00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:39.200
We'll then take a look at the various optimization view modes

14
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:43.479
Unreal Engine 5 provides to help us visually debug areas

15
00:00:43.479 --> 00:00:47.679
that could be prone to performance or optimization

16
00:00:47.679 --> 00:00:51.560
issues, and help us provide better ideas on how

17
00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:54.759
to go about solving those performance or optimization

18
00:00:54.759 --> 00:00:55.759
issues.

19
00:00:55.759 --> 00:00:58.439
Finally, we'll take a look at the number of tools

20
00:00:58.439 --> 00:01:02.280
Unreal Engine 5 provides to help us optimize our projects

21
00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:05.200
no matter which platform we happen to be developing for.

22
00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.239
We've got a lot to cover, so let's go ahead

23
00:01:07.239 --> 00:01:11.120
and get started with optimization philosophy.
